Fiete Hopf, the 29-year-old conductor almost lost his canvas shoes when directing the orchestra with his wild-fashioned gestures.
It's Monday night, the Imbongi choir repeated a new song in Heidelberg's Institute of Medical Psychology.
Fifty singers aged between 23 and '69 came, from geneticist in human medicine to man at home.
"Om'Obani" is not an elegant song, every singer has different lyrics, all in a very exotic language: zulu, a language spoken by 11 million people in South Africa, Botswana, Lesotho, Malawi, Mozambique and some parts of Swaziland.
Being helped to help each other
